  "style": {
    "id": "fogged-glass",
    "name": "Fogged Glass",
    "description": "A steamed-up window pane: behind it a bright sunrise town (sky, balloons, skyline, river, lamps) painted once into a sharp texture and once into a pre-blurred, milky, bokeh-dotted 'fogged' texture. An unseen finger writes in the condensation: the fog mask is a pure function of t — for every pixel, clear = max over planned strokes of (drawn by now x re-fogging decay), redrawn from the plan each frame into a small mask canvas (no accumulation). The pane shader shows the fogged texture where the mask is 0 and the sharp scene where it is 1, with a beaded boundary, a refracting lit/shaded water rim along every wiped edge, a wet sheen on fresh strokes and lens-like drops that gather under the strokes and run down with stick-slip, leaving clear trails. Old strokes narrow and fog over; a palm sweep clears the whole pane and the last fog evaporates. Squeaks, drip plinks, the palm swipe and the reveal chime come from the same plan (fogplan.js).",
